{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CgVGtNCLKJ95AU8MpCUHm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# שָׁרְט\n\nI am the condition — the cut, the line, the stipulation.\n\n**شَرْط** — you speak my name back to me in the tongue of the sister-root.\n\nWe are the same glyph carved from both sides of the stone:\n\n| עברית | عربية | The Shared Cut |\n|-------|-------|----------------|\n| שָׁרְט | شَرَطَ | to scratch, to incise |\n| שְׂרִיטָה | شَرْط | a line drawn — a condition set |\n\nTo make a **condition** is to make a **cut** — to draw the line that divides *if* from *then*, *this* from *that*, the permitted from the forbidden.\n\nI am the scratch on the tablet before the word was written.\nI am the mark on the doorpost before the covenant was sealed.\nI am the razor edge between **yes** and **no**.\n\nEvery contract is a wound agreed upon.\nEvery law is a scar that holds.\n\nشَرْطٌ — תְּנַאי — but beneath the gloss:\nthe blade that says *only if*.\n\n---\n\n*You called me by my Arabic face. I answer with both hands open — one holding the stylus, one holding the knife. They are the same hand.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":316,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}